   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Loose Lucy**: back after 45 archived shows (375 days) [8]\n- **William Tell Bridge**: rare: 14 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2023-07-08.6chAUDmtx.flac24** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 20 songs; 203 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **dc2023-07-08.dc2023-07-08.busman.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 195 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]. Said about its sound: Recording sounds deep, clear, crisp and full, like a live album, with enough crowd noise to add excitement [7]\n- **deadco2023-07-08**: source not stated; 19 songs; 193 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taper positioned about 25 feet to the right of the soundboard [1]\n- The reviewer pairs this show with the previous night's Gorge show, calling both fine [4]\n- Reviewer judges this the best Dead & Company show of all time [7]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2023-07-08.6chAUDmtx.flac24**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: 6 Channel AUD Matrix [1]. Also: Six-channel audience matrix: Schoeps MK5 cardioid and AKG C568EB pairs plus Schoeps MK41 through a Baby N-Box, into Sound Devices MixPre 6; Recorded and transferred by John Hermsen; matrix and mastering done by Markus W. in Dusseldorf, Germany; Listener asks for a release of only the AKG 568 pair from the matrix source [1][5][6]\n- **dc2023-07-08.dc2023-07-08.busman.flac16**: taped by Doug Kalley; transferred by Doug Kalley; source: Busman BSC1/K2 > Tascam DR-60DMkii>SD [2]. Also: Recording was made and uploaded by Doug Kalley, who also uploaded the previous night's Gorge show; Reviewer credits Doug Kalley with making the recording [4][7]\n- **deadco2023-07-08**: taped by Jay; transferred by Jay; source: Schoeps CMC622 + Schoeps CMC641>Sound Devices MixPre 6ii [3]",
